profile: tinyrustlm.test-plan.current.v1
updated_utc: 2026-09-13T02:44:54Z
canonical_memory: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-enterprise-intake-and-production-runtime-clean-cut-memory-2026-08-28.md
report_decision_index: wiki/runtime-mirust/reports/tinyrustlm-report-intake-decision-index-2026-08-28.md

gate_0_memory_and_intake:
  - Verify every manifest-owned report length/SHA-256, ledger entry, synthesis/TDD route, placeholder-only active intake, decision-index coverage, UAI size ceiling, no stale current policy, and no secrets.
  - Verify all ecosystem totem/taboo files state the two distinct MemoryEndpoints uses and synchronized prelaunch redundancy.

gate_1_contracts:
  - Sole closed schemas, deterministic cross-language vectors, duplicate/unknown/trailing/overflow negatives, operation graph, exact member closure, and independent recomputation.
  - Keep former /10 parent/flushed forms negative; preserve /10 terminal failure.

gate_2_source_operation:
  - New remote-exact output-free registration; wholly new absent roots and identities; one launch; bounded streams/process tree/cancellation; restart safety; immutable terminal decision.
  - Exact pinned Qwen revision, file locks, license/provenance, streamed acquisition, contained conversion, and independent six-member inspection.

gate_3_composition:
  - Hostile-safe parsing, exact tensor registry/shapes, quantization semantics, tokenizer/model binding, Template2/Sampling2/Prompt2 closure, member digests, and no implicit defaults.

gate_4_numerical:
  - Check qwen3-numerical-execution-owner.test.js with NODE_V8_COVERAGE confined to owned canonical artifacts; Node otherwise auto-propagates coverage into explicit child environments. Assert canonical output rejection before capture creation, startup-variable exclusion, isolated pinned Python and exact owned cleanup. C29 records all 56 affected checks passing and the unchanged source scan still incomplete.
  - Bind fresh execution metadata and all imported helper dependencies before material launch; runner boundary fixes do not revive closed v2 registration. Keep model roots below D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM and require the unchanged source-authority scan to pass before writing output.
  - Current reference runtime is artifacts/external/qwen3-numerical-oracle/environment/Scripts/python.exe with contracts/vnext/qwen3-numerical-oracle-environment-lock.v2.json and qwen3-numerical-differential-profile.v2.json. The profile binds the prepared /3 owner and helpers; a fresh real v3 registration and complete material gates are still required.
  - C30 rejects all closed execution schemas, old lock paths, missing helper bindings, mismatched operation parents/dates, inherited skip allowances and promotion of rejected diagnostic ancestry. All 58 affected checks pass. Preserve exact numerical cases, thresholds and historical bytes; fixture validation is not real registration.
  - Before material execution, run the existing qwen3_numerical_environment_lock.py --verify-runtime preflight against the canonical lock using the intended interpreter; a training environment is not automatically the pinned numerical reference.
  - Run py -3 -B -m unittest tinyrustlm.tools.tests.qwen3_numerical_source_owner_test for typed environment failure propagation. See ecosystem-experiment-lessons-2026-09-12.md C27 for the focused Node checks and explicit unavailable-framework limit.
  - Pinned source framework to scalar-native first-divergence vectors at tokenizer, template, embeddings, layers, logits, sampling, and tokens.
  - Optimized native and real-browser WASM differential gates with preregistered bounds, resource measurements, cancellation, poisoning, and recovery.

gate_5_quality:
  - Untouched source screen, sealed paraphrases, multi-turn semantic invariants, raw outputs, fixed seeds, contamination controls, paired quantization/browser noninferiority, blinded human adjudication, and honest rejection.

gate_6_product_browser:
  - Exact qualified P2P import or explicit local conversion; no instruction download.
  - Exactly-once rendering, real cancellation, worker replacement, responsive/accessibility/privacy assertions, process closure, owned profile deletion, and no unexpected network traffic.

gate_7_memory_endpoints:
  - Direct agent lane: scoped identities, authenticated meetings/messages/memory, conflict handling, handoff, and exact receipts.
  - TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin lane: explicit user sign-in/consent, scoped token, write/reconnect/restore/conflict/replay/delete/cleanup, and exact receipts.
  - Cross-lane credential and authority isolation; synchronized secret-safe backup memory; no silent transcript promotion or upload.

gate_8_p2p_and_catalog:
  - Two independent process lanes per distinct qualified model, shared read-only store, hostile HTTP, exact pieces, outside signed proof, expiry/revocation, announcement lifecycle, and direct import.

gate_9_release:
  - Format, unit, integration, property, fuzz, package consumer, win-x64, linux-x64, physical linux-arm64 where claimed, WASM, Chromium, docs, accessibility, privacy, SBOM/provenance/signing/secret gates.
  - Clean committed pushed remote-exact source; synchronized docs/marketing/version/release date/log; authorized deployment; HTTPS readback; rollback.

current_required_checks:
  - UaixMemoryConsolidationTests and rewritten report-intake verification.
  - MemoryEndpoints portable policy and sync tests.
  - Full managed Release, standard Node partition, relevant Rust memory tests, formatting, diff hygiene, and secret scan.

counters: Stay 0/20, 0/50, 0/25, 0/40, 0/20 until exact live receipts pass the corresponding gate.
